  "reason": "The records collectively point toward the result: R6 supplies the closely related lamellar FCC/B2 eutectic alloy, R4 demonstrates combined high-pressure/high-temperature treatment of an HEA, R1 connects coherent multiscale structures with strength–ductility synergy, and R18 demonstrates hierarchical decomposition in a closely related Al–Co–Cr–Fe–Ni alloy family. Pressure-assisted routes such as HIP, SPS, and HPT provide additional related processing precedent. However, none of the records specifically teaches using a hexahedron-anvil HPHT treatment to convert the Al0.7CoCrFeNi lamellae into a coherent hierarchical FCC/B2 pattern, nor do they establish preferential FCC-to-B2 dislocation transfer as the stress-relief mechanism. Combining these elements would therefore require a substantial new idea rather than a straightforward reconstruction."
